  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While it's a good step to make it so that people can no longer rename themselves to things that have non-alphabetical characters in their names other than those of syllabary languages like Chinese and Korean; that doesn't change the fact that plenty of people still have such characters in their names, or that have names made up entirely of those characters; allowing them to continue to abuse the report system glitches associated with those characters.\nUnless the team plans to fix said glitches and bring back all unicode characters for all users; I believe it would be more prudent to force users with such characters still in their names to do a rename the next time they log in, with the naming cooldown dismissed if they were still on it.",
